The count of even regions\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "vector< Edge > Isotopy::Graph::flippable_edges ()"

.PP
Returns all Q1 edges in the current triangulation that can be flipped\&. Requires \fBprepare()\fP to have been called\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Vector of all flippable Q1 edges\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void Isotopy::Graph::initialize (const vector< bool > & sign_vector)"

.PP
Initializes the graph structure from a sign vector\&. Sets up quadrant indices, polarisation array, antipodal partners, and reserves space for edge vectors\&. Must be called before \fBprocess_triangles()\fP or \fBprocess_edges()\fP\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsign_vector\fP The sign vector with a boolean value for each vertex\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "bool Isotopy::Graph::is_flippable (const Edge & edge)"

.PP
Returns true if the given Q1 edge can be flipped\&. An edge is flippable if it is interior (has a twin) and the resulting quadrilateral is strictly convex\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIedge\fP The Q1 edge to test\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if the edge can be flipped, false otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "bool Isotopy::Graph::is_mcurve ()\fR [inline]\fP"

.PP
Checks if the graph represents an M-curve\&. An M-curve is characterized by having the maximal possible number of regions for the given degree\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if the graph is an M-curve, false otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void Isotopy::Graph::isotopy_type ()"

.PP
Computes the full isotopy type of the graph\&. This is the recommended entry point for users, and the core of the library\&. It runs the whole pipeline: connected components, isotopy root detection, region calculation, and region sign assignment\&. After calling this function, all relevant isotopy invariants and structures are available for further queries\&.

.PP
The isotopy root is the component containing a side point connected to its antipode, indicating that the isotopy process has merged all relevant regions\&. It is detected by a bipartiteness check over the antipodal pairs for even degree, by an antipodal conflict for odd degree, and by a same-region adjacency edge as the odd-degree fallback\&.

.PP
Regions are then formed by union-find over antipodal connections, grouping components that are connected via antipodes into the same region; this also builds region_adjacency and determines root_region\&.

.PP
Calling this function repeatedly is cheap: it returns immediately once the isotopy type has been computed, until invalidated by \fBupdate_edge()\fP or \fBupdate_sign()\fP\&.

.PP
\fBExceptions\fP
.RS 4
\fIstd::runtime_error\fP if no isotopy root is found\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int Isotopy::Graph::odd_regions ()\fR [inline]\fP"

.PP
Returns the number of odd regions in the isotopy decomposition\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The count of odd regions\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void Isotopy::Graph::prepare (const vector< Triangle > & triangles)"

.PP
Sets up the DCEL and edge lookup structures\&. Must be called before update_edge(edge) or \fBis_flippable()\fP\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItriangles\fP The Q1 triangulation (same list used to construct the graph)\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void Isotopy::Graph::process_edges (const vector< Edge > & edges)"

.PP
Processes edges to populate component and adjacency edges\&. Must be called after \fBinitialize()\fP\&. Classifies edges as same-sign (component edges) or different-sign (adjacency edges) across all quadrants\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIedges\fP The list of edges, each represented as a pair of vertex indices\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void Isotopy::Graph::process_triangles (const vector< Triangle > & triangles)"

.PP
Processes triangles to populate component and adjacency edges\&. Must be called after \fBinitialize()\fP\&. Classifies triangle edges as same-sign (component edges) or different-sign (adjacency edges) across all quadrants\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItriangles\fP The list of triangles, each represented as three vertex indices\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void Isotopy::Graph::update_edge (const Edge & edge)"

.PP
Flips the given Q1 edge if it is flippable\&. Does nothing if the edge is not flippable\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIedge\fP The Q1 edge to flip\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void Isotopy::Graph::update_sign (int vector_index)"

.PP
Updates the sign of a vertex and invalidates cached computation results\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvector_index\fP The index of the vertex in the polarisation array whose sign is toggled\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "string Isotopy::Graph::viro_notation (bool unicode = \fRfalse\fP)"

.PP
Returns the Viro notation for the isotopy type of the graph\&. Generates a string representation (Viro notation) of the isotopy type, using the computed regions and their adjacencies\&. Optionally outputs Unicode symbols for delimiters and separators\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIunicode\fP If true, use Unicode symbols; otherwise, use ASCII\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The Viro notation string for the isotopy type\&. 
.RE
.PP


